=== MDV-P2-011
title: Medication reconciliation: chart vs patient-reported vs other source, keep / change / stop (E-07)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E04
prd: P2-04
screens: E-07
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: reconciliation, medicines, safety
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 12
depends: MDV-P2-008
confidence: 86 | Hi-fi reconciliation table with decisions and disabled confirm until all decided.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Clinical Screens (E-07); docs/02-design/source/Medvya Gap Analysis (Medication reconciliation, MUST)
desc:
Reconciliation table: medicine, chart, patient-reported, other source (HIS column hidden until P7), conflict flag, decision Keep / Change / Stop (patient-only items: Add / Ignore). Summary "n of m decided · k sources disagree". "Confirm changes" disabled until every row has a decision; confirmed decisions update MEDICATION_STATEMENT review_state and feed the Rx composer (stop → discontinue line).
ac:
- Confirm is disabled until all rows are decided (UI + API).
- Each decision records actor, time and reason for Stop/Change; history is kept.
- Conflicts are flagged with text (e.g. "atorvastatin active in chart, patient says stopped").
- Stopped medicines show as stopped with date in Patient 360 and the timeline.

=== MDV-P2-012
title: Sign and finalise: immutable signed note v1 with re-authentication (E-06)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E04
prd: P2-05
screens: E-06
covers: exit:3
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: signing, immutability, ledger
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 12-13
depends: MDV-P2-009, MDV-P1-007
confidence: 90 | Sign modal copy and immutability rule fully specified; ledger approach in ADR-006.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Clinician App (sign modal, signed banner); docs/adr/ADR-006-immutable-signed-records.md
desc:
Sign modal: "Sign note for {name}? MRN · DOB · encounter id. I have reviewed every section … read-only after signing. Prescriptions and orders are authorised separately." CTA "Sign as Dr. {name}" requires passkey/MFA step-up. Signed NOTE_VERSION v1 is stored in a hash-chained table (MDV-P0-036) with document hash; banner "SIGNED v1 · read-only" and signer line with licence number and time.
ac:
- Only a doctor with a verified licence and care relationship can sign; step-up authentication is required within the last 5 minutes.
- After signing, the note body cannot be modified through any API; an automated test attempts direct API and repository updates and both fail (exit gate 3).
- The stored document hash verifies against the rendered content; ledger verification passes.
- Signing writes NoteSigned.v1 (no PHI) and an audit event; Today removes it from pending notes.

=== MDV-P2-013
title: Addenda, version history and print/PDF of the signed note (E-06)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E04
prd: P2-05
screens: E-06
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: signing, addendum, print
estimate: 2
weeks: 13
depends: MDV-P2-012
confidence: 88 | Designed (addendum composer → sign; version history; A4 print header rule).
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Clinical Screens (E-06); docs/02-design/source/Medvya Wireframes (E-06)
desc:
Addendum composer on a signed note creates a new signed version (amends_version_id, reason) with the same sign flow; version history lists v1, v2… with signer and time. Print/PDF: A4, header with patient name, MRN and DOB on every page, signer block, version, "Corrections are added as signed addenda".
ac:
- An addendum never alters v1; viewing shows the original plus addenda in order.
- Addendum requires a reason and step-up authentication.
- PDF renders server-side with MRN/DOB on every page and is stored with hash.
- Print view passes screen-reader and 200 % zoom checks.

=== MDV-P2-014
title: Country formulary and order sets: India (Schedule H/H1/X) and UAE drug codes, admin add medicine (F-13)
type: Story
