=== MDV-P2-029
title: Encounters start race: a second start that loses the race answers with the winner's encounter
type: Task
epic: MDV-P2-E04
prd: P2-04
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: encounters, domain
estimate: 0.5
weeks: 9
depends: MDV-P2-001
confidence: 95 | Cause reproduced by a forced-interleaving test on real PostgreSQL.
sources: src/Modules/Encounters/Medvya.Encounters.Infrastructure/EncounterService.cs; tests/Medvya.IntegrationTests/EncounterTests.cs
desc:
Two starts of the same visit at the same moment (double click, two tabs) could fail: the losing start read no encounter for the visit, then the winner committed, then the loser's open-consultation check found the winner's encounter for this same visit and refused with "another consultation is open". The open-consultation check now ignores this visit's own encounter, so the loser goes on to the insert, meets the unique index and answers with the winner.
ac:
- A start that reads no encounter for the visit and then loses the race to another start of the same visit answers with the winner's encounter, not "another consultation is open".
- A start whose insert meets the unique index answers with the winner's encounter (row-level security still applies to the re-read).
- The visit moves to In consult once and the board is told once.
- The lost-race interleavings are forced in the test (not left to parallel timing) and the test fails when the fix is removed.

@epic MDV-P2-E07 | Consultation and chart upgrade | P2-02, P2-04, P2-06 | One-page chart by life stage (adult, pregnancy, child, older adult), one-page consultation and a full Add medicine flow with patient-aware safety checks (design of 12 Nov 2026).

