=== MDV-P2-031
title: More vitals and key labs on the chart, each flagged against its reference range
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-02, P2-03
screens: E-01, N-01
priority: MUST
roles: Nurse, Doctor
labels: chart, vitals, domain
estimate: 2
weeks: 15
depends: MDV-P2-007
confidence: 85 | Observation storage exists; new codes and adult reference ranges are a small extension. Ranges need clinical sign-off.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (chartVals vitals and labs); src/Modules/Encounters/Medvya.Encounters.Domain/ChartFacts.cs
desc:
Add observation codes for height, respiratory rate, pain score, standing blood pressure, fundal height and fetal heart rate, and the key labs LDL cholesterol, eGFR, urine albumin/creatinine ratio, haemoglobin, ferritin, potassium, sodium, TSH, vitamin D and platelets. BMI is calculated from the latest weight and height, never stored as typed. Each code has a fixed unit and a reference range; a reading outside it is flagged in words (High, Low, with the range) on the chart. Nurse intake can enter height and respiratory rate. Patient 360 returns the latest reading and the trend for every code that has readings.
ac:
- Every new code has one unit and a reference range, and a value outside the range is returned with a High or Low flag and the range text.
- BMI is shown only when a weight and a height exist, uses the latest of each and states the date of the older one.
- Nurse intake saves height and respiratory rate with the same refusal of impossible values as the other vitals.
- Patient 360 returns a trend for each code with two or more readings, oldest first, with the source of each point.
- shortcut: reference ranges are one adult set (children's vitals keep the age bands of #956) and wait for clinical sign-off.

=== MDV-P2-032
title: Life stage, history sections and the fuller chart banner
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-02
screens: E-01
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Nurse
labels: chart, domain
estimate: 2
weeks: 15
depends: MDV-P2-004
confidence: 85 | Life stage is a pure rule on age and an open pregnancy; history is structured text with author and time.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (chartVals P.*.stage, hx, banner)
desc:
The chart works out the patient's life stage: child under 18, pregnancy while a pregnancy is open (MDV-P2-034), older adult from 65, otherwise adult. The life stage drives the chart module, the consultation template and the safety checks, and is shown as a label with an icon and words, not colour alone. History is kept in sections (past medical, surgical, family, social, women's health or obstetric, birth and feeding for a child, function and falls for an older adult), each with who wrote it and when. The banner adds blood group, preferred language, the care team and the consent state.
ac:
- The life stage rule is tested at the edges: 17 y 364 d is a child, 18 y is an adult, 65 y is an older adult, and an open pregnancy wins over adult.
- A doctor or nurse can edit each history section; every save records the author and time and the previous text is kept.
- The banner shows blood group and language only when recorded; nothing is guessed.
- The history sections offered depend on the life stage (birth for a child, function for an older adult).

=== MDV-P2-033
title: Patient chart on one page (E-01 redesign) with section filters and a life-stage module
type: Story
