desc:
Patient 360 becomes one page: banner (name, age, date of birth, MRN, blood group, language, life-stage label, allergy chip, alerts, care team, consent); vitals strip of six tiles with a trend line and a flag; problems with ICD-10 codes; medicines with "Add medicine" (MDV-P2-039); the life-stage module; results and trends table; history; timeline; and a right column for care gaps, goals (MDV-P2-038) and documents. Section buttons show everything or one part. Empty, loading, error and no-access states as today.
ac:
- Every block shows its data source as today (provenance tags) and an empty state when there is nothing.
- The section buttons filter the page and are keyboard operable; the choice is kept per user in the session only.
- The page works at 375 px (one column), 200 % zoom and right to left in Arabic; axe has no violations.
- A user without clinical access sees the banner and the locked notice only (server decides, as today).

=== MDV-P2-034
title: Pregnancy record: dates, gestation, obstetric history, antenatal contacts and danger signs
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-02
screens: E-01
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Nurse
labels: chart, pregnancy, domain
estimate: 3
weeks: 16
depends: MDV-P2-032
confidence: 78 | Date rules are standard (Naegele, scan dating); the antenatal contact plan follows the WHO 8-contact model and needs clinical sign-off.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (chartVals preg, ANC, danger); Medvya Foundations (PREGNANCY_EPISODE)
desc:
PREGNANCY_EPISODE per patient: last menstrual period, dating scan date and gestation at the scan, due date (LMP + 280 days, or from the scan when the scan differs by more than the dating rule), gravida, para, abortions and living children, blood group and Rh, and an outcome that closes it. Gestation today is worked out from the due date in the facility time zone. Antenatal contacts (8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 36, 38, 40 weeks) show as done, today or to come, linked to visits. Danger signs counselled are recorded with who and when. The chart shows the pregnancy module and the life stage becomes Pregnancy.
ac:
- Due date and gestation are tested: LMP 19 May 2026 gives due date 23 Feb 2027 and 24 w 3 d on 06 Nov 2026.
- A scan date that moves the due date records which date is used and why; the earlier date is kept.
- Only one open pregnancy per patient; closing it needs an outcome and the life stage returns to adult.
- Pregnancy data is SensitiveHealth, tenant isolated (EF filter and RLS) and never in logs or URLs.
- shortcut: the dating rule and the contact plan are the WHO model and wait for clinical sign-off.

=== MDV-P2-035
title: Child growth: measurements and WHO centiles with a growth chart
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-02
screens: E-01
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Nurse
labels: chart, paediatrics, domain
estimate: 3
weeks: 16
depends: MDV-P2-031, MDV-P2-032
confidence: 72 | The LMS method is standard; the reference tables must be the published WHO data, checked against WHO examples, and clinically signed off.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (growth chart, growthMeta); WHO Child Growth Standards (0–5 years)
desc:
GROWTH_MEASUREMENT: weight, length or height and head circumference with date, from nurse intake or the chart. Centiles and z-scores for weight-for-age, length/height-for-age and BMI-for-age from 0 to 5 years by sex use the WHO LMS tables. The chart draws the 3rd, 15th, 50th, 85th and 97th lines with the child's points, states the centile in words and flags a crossing of two major centile lines or a fall below the 3rd. Weight velocity is shown between the last two weights.
ac:
- The z-score calculation reproduces WHO's published examples to two decimals (test).
- The growth chart has a text alternative stating the latest centile and the trend.
- A child over 5 years shows the measurements without centiles and says why.
- shortcut: 0–5 y WHO only; IAP 2015 (5–18 y, India) and UAE national charts when the clinical reviewer chooses them. The tables wait for clinical sign-off.

=== MDV-P2-036
title: Immunisations against the country schedule, and developmental milestones
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-02
screens: E-01
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Nurse
labels: chart, paediatrics, domain
estimate: 3
weeks: 16
depends: MDV-P2-032
confidence: 70 | Recording is simple; the IAP 2023 and UAE schedules in the design are marked "verify" and need clinical sign-off before use.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (imm, miles); Medvya Foundations (IMMUNIZATION, DEVELOPMENTAL_MILESTONE)
desc:
IMMUNIZATION: vaccine, dose, date given, batch, who gave it, or deferred with a reason. The country schedule (India IAP 2023, UAE national) is a country rule class; the chart lists each age band as given, due now, overdue or upcoming from the child's date of birth. DEVELOPMENTAL_MILESTONE: per age band, each milestone answered yes, no or unsure, with who answered (parent or clinician). Vaccines due feed the care gaps (MDV-P2-038).
ac:
- The schedule is chosen by the facility's country through a country rule class, never an if on the country.
- Due and overdue are worked out from the date of birth in the facility time zone and tested at the band edges.
- Deferring a dose needs a reason; nothing is deleted.
- shortcut: the schedules are the design's reading of IAP 2023 and the UAE schedule and are marked unverified until clinical sign-off.

=== MDV-P2-037
title: Older adult review: falls, walking test, standing blood pressure drop, frailty, memory, daily activities and a medicine review
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-02
screens: E-01
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Nurse
labels: chart, geriatrics, domain
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 16
depends: MDV-P2-031, MDV-P2-032
confidence: 76 | Scores are standard instruments; flag lines (TUG over 12 s, a 20/10 mmHg drop) and the Beers subset need clinical sign-off.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (geri, deprescribe); Medvya Foundations (GERIATRIC_ASSESSMENT)
desc:
GERIATRIC_ASSESSMENT with date and author: falls in 12 months, Timed Up and Go seconds, lying and standing blood pressure (the drop is calculated and flagged as orthostatic at 20 systolic or 10 diastolic), Clinical Frailty Scale 1–9, Mini-Cog 0–5, ADL and IADL, PHQ-2 and a nutrition note. The medicine review lists suggestions from a small rule set (benzodiazepines, a proton pump inhibitor for more than 8 weeks, oral NSAIDs, and an ACE inhibitor or ARB with low eGFR and high potassium) as "suggestions, the doctor decides", each with a "plan change" action.
ac:
- Each score is refused outside its scale and the orthostatic drop is tested at the flag line.
- The medicine review never changes a medicine by itself; a planned change goes to the consultation plan.
- shortcut: the flag lines and the rule set wait for clinical sign-off.

=== MDV-P2-038
title: Chronic care targets, care gaps due today and care-plan goals
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-02
screens: E-01
priority: SHOULD
roles: Doctor
labels: chart, care-gaps, domain
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 16
depends: MDV-P2-031, MDV-P2-034, MDV-P2-036
confidence: 74 | The gap rules are a short, explicit list; which ones the pilot doctors want is a clinical choice.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (targets, gaps, goals)
desc:
Targets per patient for HbA1c, blood pressure, LDL, eGFR and urine albumin, with defaults the doctor can change; the chart shows each latest value against its target. Care gaps come from rules: diabetic eye and foot checks once a year, urine albumin once a year for diabetes, a test ordered but never resulted, vaccines due (MDV-P2-036), the glucose tolerance test window at 24–28 weeks of pregnancy, and a falls review after a fall. Each gap has an action (add to today's visit, order, refer). Care-plan goals are text with a target and progress.
ac:
- Each gap rule is tested for due, not due and done.
- A gap's action adds the item to the open consultation's plan; with no open consultation it says so.
- shortcut: the gap rules are the design's list and wait for clinical sign-off.

=== MDV-P2-039
title: Add medicine panel from the chart and the consultation: strength, how often, when, how long, instructions, line and quantity
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-06
screens: E-05, E-11
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: prescribing, ui
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 15
depends: MDV-P2-015, MDV-P2-016
confidence: 84 | The composer, sig and checks exist; this is a faster entry path over them.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (Add medicine drawer, medVals)
desc:
A side panel opened from the chart's Medicines card and the consultation plan: search the formulary (brand or generic), choose the strength, how often (1-0-0, 0-0-1, 1-0-1, 1-1-1, when needed, weekly), when (before food, after food, bedtime, any time), for how long (3 days, 5 days, 1 month, 3 months, ongoing) and the patient instructions. It shows the patient (name, age, the context that drives the checks) and the allergy chip, the safety checks for this line (MDV-P2-016, MDV-P2-040), the finished prescription line and the quantity. "Add to prescription" adds the line to the encounter's draft prescription; a severe finding blocks it until another medicine is chosen or an override reason is given.
ac:
- The quantity is calculated from frequency and duration (when needed: one pack) and tested.
- The line uses the existing sig, so print and share are unchanged.
- From the chart without an open consultation, the panel says a consultation must be started; nothing is prescribed outside an encounter.
- Keyboard path, 44 px targets, English and Arabic right to left, axe clean.

=== MDV-P2-040
title: Patient-aware prescribing checks: pregnancy, weight-based child dose, kidney function and older adult
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-06
screens: E-11
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: safety, prescribing
estimate: 3
weeks: 15-16
depends: MDV-P2-016, MDV-P2-031, MDV-P2-032
confidence: 70 | The check logic is clear; the rules are a curated pilot set, not a licensed knowledge base, and need clinical sign-off.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (medVals checks per patient); src/Modules/Prescribing/Medvya.Prescribing.Domain/SafetyChecks.cs
desc:
The safety checks read the patient context: pregnancy and gestation (NSAIDs from 20 weeks severe), the latest weight no older than one month for a child (dose per kg and per day, worked out in mg and, for a liquid, in mL; over the maximum is severe), the latest eGFR (NSAIDs and metformin thresholds), and age 65 or over (a small Beers subset as moderate). Missing context (no weight, no eGFR) is reported as "not checked" with the reason, never as safe. The rule set version is raised and recorded with each check and override.
ac:
- A seeded set (ibuprofen at 24 weeks, paracetamol 15 mg/kg at 14.2 kg = 213 mg = 8.9 mL of 120 mg/5 mL, diclofenac tablets with eGFR 52 and losartan, diazepam at 76) gives the expected finding in every case (automated test).
- A child dose without a weight from the last month is not checked, and says so.
- Each new finding is mutation checked: the test fails when the rule is removed.
- shortcut: a curated pilot rule set waiting for the clinical safety reviewer (MDV-P2-028); a licensed knowledge base later.

=== MDV-P2-041
title: Consultation on one page (E-04 redesign) with the guided steps kept as an option
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-04
screens: E-04
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: encounters, ui
estimate: 3
weeks: 15-16
depends: MDV-P2-009, MDV-P2-012
confidence: 82 | The note, autosave, consent, assist and sign already work; this is a new layout over them.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (CONSULTATION STUDIO, studioVals)
desc:
The consultation opens as one page: the patient strip with life stage and allergies, the recording consent bar first (patient agreed, declined so the doctor types, consent withdrawn while listening), then numbered sections Vitals, History, the adaptive template (MDV-P2-042), Examination, Assessment, Plan (MDV-P2-043) and Review and sign (MDV-P2-044), with a section bar that stays at the top and ticks each finished section. A switch flips to the existing guided steps; nothing of the old flow is lost. The right panel has Assist suggestions, a chart summary and the checklist.
ac:
- The one-page and guided views save the same note; switching keeps every typed word (autosave as today).
- The section bar is a nav landmark with links that move focus to the section; ticks are icon and words.
- Declined consent hides Assist and keeps the manual note path as today.
- Desktop two columns, phone one column, Arabic right to left, axe clean.

=== MDV-P2-042
title: Structured review of systems and examination, and a template chosen by the patient
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-04
screens: E-04
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: encounters, templates, domain
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 16
depends: MDV-P2-025, MDV-P2-032
confidence: 80 | Templates are versioned already; new versions carry the structured sections.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (ros, exam, tpl per patient)
desc:
New template versions add a review of systems (each symptom yes or no, unanswered stays blank) and an examination by body system (Normal, Abnormal with a note, Not examined). The consultation suggests a template from the life stage and problems: diabetes review for diabetes, antenatal for a pregnancy, paediatrics for a child and a new older-adult review (standing blood pressure, walking test, frailty, home safety) for an older adult; the doctor can change it. Released versions stay pinned on old notes. The signed note and its PDF show the structured answers in words.
ac:
- An unanswered symptom or system stays blank in the signed note; nothing defaults to normal.
- Abnormal needs a note; Not examined is printed as such.
- The suggested template is tested per life stage, and the doctor's choice wins.
- Old notes keep their template version (fingerprint test unchanged for released versions).

=== MDV-P2-043
title: Plan section: medicine actions, tests to order, advice in the patient's language, follow-up and referral
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-04, P2-06
screens: E-04, E-05
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: encounters, prescribing, ui
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 16
depends: MDV-P2-011, MDV-P2-018, MDV-P2-019, MDV-P2-039
confidence: 80 | Reconciliation, orders and referrals exist; change and taper are new reconciliation actions.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (rx, inv, advice, fu)
desc:
The plan shows the prescription with an action per medicine: continue, new, change (new dose), taper (a stepped dose with an end date) or stop, using the reconciliation and the composer. Tests are toggles that create draft orders. Advice for the patient is written once and printed and sent in the patient's language when a reviewed translation exists, otherwise in English with a note. Follow-up is a choice (for example 2 weeks, 1 month, 3 months) that the front desk sees as a booking to make. Referral opens the existing referral letter.
ac:
- Change and taper are recorded on the reconciliation with the old and new dose and print on the prescription.
- A test toggled on creates a draft order once; toggling off removes the draft, not an ordered one.
- The follow-up choice appears on the front desk's list for that patient.

=== MDV-P2-044
title: Review and sign checklist: signing stays locked until every item is reviewed
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E07
prd: P2-05
screens: E-04, E-06
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: encounters, safety
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 16
depends: MDV-P2-012, MDV-P2-041
confidence: 84 | Signing and step-up exist; the checklist adds explicit gates the server checks.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (CK checklist, remLine, canSign)
desc:
The checklist: identity confirmed, allergies reconciled, medicines reconciled, recording consent recorded, history reviewed, every AI suggestion accepted or dismissed, diagnoses reviewed and plan reviewed. The Sign button stays locked and says how many items remain. The server refuses a signature while an AI draft or suggestion is still undecided or consent is unrecorded, so the lock is not only the screen. After signing, changes go in as an addendum, as today.
ac:
- Signing with an undecided AI suggestion is refused by the server (test, mutation checked).
- The remaining count and each item are announced to screen readers.
- The checklist state is derived from the note, never stored separately.

