desc:
Programme: MDV-P1-E12 · UX programme: safe, cohesive clinic workspace (from the Nov 2026 product UX audit). Track D (design rules and UI component setup), wave D3. This is audit backlog UX-19 of the Nov 2026 product UX audit (an audit id, not an MDV key).

Persona and route: /front-desk · receptionist.
Findings and reviewers: F-12 · reviewers B-02, B-06, C-23 · arbitration ruling 4.
Rationale: The board shows about one and a half cards per column on a first screen; a grouped list shows about nine patients in the same space. The arbitration keeps the board for the pilot and adds the list later as a choice.
Proposed UX behaviour: A third view, List, in the view switch. Rows grouped by status in the order of who needs action: waiting, with nurse, in consult, then booked, then done (collapsed). Status counts above the list act as filters. Each row: token, patient name, flags, wait, the doctor, one action; rows are 48 px (comfortable), actions 44 px, never compact. Order within a group follows the clinic's queue rule and matches the display. Undo sits in the toolbar. Check-in from a search result keeps the identity confirmation (name and date of birth) and shows the doctor being assigned. By status and By doctor stay; each receptionist's last choice is the default for her.
Prototype and blueprint reference: docs/product-ux-audit/concepts/medvya-workspace-concept.html, receptionist view (audit notes 8, 9 and 10); screenshots docs/product-ux-audit/concepts/screenshots/desk-1440.png, desk-1024.png, desk-768.png, desk-375.png, desk-1440-annotated.png. The concept's 40 px rows and Booked first are not built: see the rulings.
Components and tokens affected: QueueTable, SegmentedControl, Chip, the table controller. No new component.
Front end and back end split: Front end only (the board object and live feed are view-agnostic).
Prerequisites and blocked by: Blocked by the undo ticket, the board chrome ticket, the queue-rule ticket and the picker-rows ticket. Timing: after the first pilot weeks, or before the first staff training session if the founder moves it there; never between training and the first two pilot weeks (arbitration ruling 6).
Clinical sign-off: Decision: question 14 of the validation plan (board or list), by the receptionist, with the side-by-side of receptionist scenario step 8; recorded on the issue.
Effort and regression risk: M · Low: an added view; the board is untouched.
Deliberately NOT in this ticket: (1) Removing or replacing the board. (2) 40 px rows or any compact density on this list. (3) A single find-or-check-in box.
ac:
- Given Front desk, when the view switch is read, then By status, By doctor and List are offered and the first two behave as before
- Given 20 booked and 6 waiting patients, when the list opens, then the waiting group is first and done is collapsed
- Given the status counts, when one is pressed, then only that group shows and the pressed state is exposed to assistive technology
- Given 40 rows with long names at 1024 by 768 and 1440 by 900, when the list renders, then no text is clipped and no sideways scrolling occurs
- Given any pointer, when rows and actions are measured, then rows are at least 48 px and actions at least 44 px with at least 8 px between actions in adjacent rows
- Given a search result in the list, when Check in is pressed, then name and date of birth are confirmed first, as on the board
- Given the clinic's queue rule, when the list and the queue display are compared, then the order within a status is the same
- Given English and Arabic at 1440, 1024 and 375, when axe runs, then there is no violation
tests:
- New steps in tests/e2e/front-desk.spec.ts and fullstack/front-desk.spec.ts for the List view; J3 unchanged and green.
- A 40-row fixture from the synthetic generator.
notes:
- Regression risk: low.

=== MDV-P2-053
title: Clinic today for the owner: five counts the system can stand behind and a needs-attention list
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E12
prd: P1-08
screens: D-04
priority: SHOULD
roles: Owner, Practice admin
labels: overview, metrics, ux, settings, epic: ux programme, track: design, wave: D3
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 12
depends: MDV-P1-106, MDV-P1-090, MDV-P1-084, MDV-P1-086
confidence: 68 | Live counts need no new back end; pending lists per doctor need a query. Which five numbers the owner wants is not yet asked.
sources: docs/product-ux-audit/10-prioritized-implementation-backlog.md (audit backlog UX-22); docs/product-ux-audit/04-evidence-backed-findings.md (F-29); docs/product-ux-audit/07-debate-and-arbitration.md (ruling 7); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-a-rebuttal.md (section 6); web/clinic/src/features/front-desk/components/ClinicOverviewPage.tsx
desc:
Programme: MDV-P1-E12 · UX programme: safe, cohesive clinic workspace (from the Nov 2026 product UX audit). Track D (design rules and UI component setup), wave D3. This is audit backlog UX-22 of the Nov 2026 product UX audit (an audit id, not an MDV key).

Persona and route: A Clinic today page for the owner (in place of, or beside, Clinic overview) · owner, practice admin · phone to desktop, read only.
Findings and reviewers: F-29 · reviewer A-19 · arbitration ruling 7. Part 2 of 2 of audit backlog UX-22 (part 1 fixed the check-in timer).
Rationale: The owner, who is the buyer, has four 14-day numbers inside Settings and nothing on how the day is going. The concept showed more than the system can stand behind: seen and median consult depend on a Done state the desk could press without a doctor.
Proposed UX behaviour: One page with exactly these counts: booked today and still to arrive; arrived, split walk-in and booked; waiting now and the longest wait; notes to sign and prescriptions to authorise per doctor; registrations incomplete. Below them a needs-attention list, each line with one action (for example 3 notes unsigned from yesterday · Open). Revenue reads Not tracked yet. No seen count, median consult time, running-late figure or no-show rate until the visit states are reliable. Missing data says No data yet, never zero. The page holds counts and staff names only, no patient names.
Prototype and blueprint reference: docs/product-ux-audit/concepts/medvya-workspace-concept.html, owner view (audit notes 11 and 12); screenshots docs/product-ux-audit/concepts/screenshots/owner-1440.png, owner-1024.png, owner-768.png, owner-375.png, owner-1440-annotated.png. The concept shows more than is built: see the guide's list of what it does not settle.
Components and tokens affected: PageHeader, Card, PageMessage, Chip. No new component.
Front end and back end split: Front end for live counts; back end for the pending lists per doctor (authorised for owner and practice admin, tenant-scoped).
Prerequisites and blocked by: Blocked by the check-in timer ticket and the End-with-unfinished-prescription ticket (it provides prescriptions to authorise). Timing: after the safety tickets; before the pilot review meeting if time allows (ruling 7), otherwise after the first pilot weeks.
Clinical sign-off: Decision: question 17 of the validation plan (which five numbers the owner wants every evening), recorded on the issue. The five above are the default.
Effort and regression risk: M · Low.
Deliberately NOT in this ticket: (1) Revenue, no-shows, consult times and reports (MDV-P4-030). (2) Any figure derived from the unreliable Done state. (3) A wall of KPI cards.
ac:
- Given the page, when it is read, then it shows the five counts above and no seen, median consult, running late or revenue figure
- Given revenue, when the page renders, then it reads Not tracked yet; given a count with no data, then it reads No data yet and not 0
- Given a needs-attention line, when its action is pressed, then the matching screen opens filtered to that item
- Given the board and the doctors' days, when the counts are compared at the same moment, then they are equal
- Given a receptionist or another clinic's owner, when the page's API is called, then the server answers 403 or returns only their own clinic, and the test fails if the policy is removed
- Given the page and its API answers, when they are read, then they hold counts and staff names only
- Given 375, 768 and 1440 in English and Arabic, when axe runs, then there is no violation
tests:
- Integration: pending-per-doctor query, policy, tenant isolation.
- Playwright (tests/e2e/clinic-overview.spec.ts): the five counts, Not tracked yet, one action per line.
notes:
- Regression risk: low.

=== MDV-P2-054
title: Tables: one controller for sort and paging, stacked rows on phones, and compact density for four reference tables only
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E12
prd: P0-07
priority: SHOULD
roles: Owner, Practice admin, Doctor, Receptionist
labels: design-system, ui, a11y, responsive, epic: ux programme, track: design, wave: D3
estimate: 4
weeks: 13-14
depends: MDV-P1-077, MDV-P1-079
confidence: 68 | The Table primitive is good; 17 of 19 tables have no controller, so it is one table at a time.
sources: docs/product-ux-audit/10-prioritized-implementation-backlog.md (audit backlog UX-30); docs/product-ux-audit/04-evidence-backed-findings.md (F-24); docs/product-ux-audit/07-debate-and-arbitration.md (ruling 2); docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md (sections 4 and 9); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-c-design-system.md (C-06, C-13, section 2.5); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-b-rebuttal.md (section 4); docs/05-delivery/tickets/P0-foundation/MDV-P0-030.md; AGENTS.md (section 4)
desc:
Programme: MDV-P1-E12 · UX programme: safe, cohesive clinic workspace (from the Nov 2026 product UX audit). Track D (design rules and UI component setup), wave D3. This is audit backlog UX-30 of the Nov 2026 product UX audit (an audit id, not an MDV key).

Persona and route: Staff, audit log, formulary, order sets (compact allowed); every other table (controller, paging, stacked rows).
Findings and reviewers: F-24 · reviewers C-06, C-13.
Rationale: Staff rows are about 69 px (7 per screen); the audit table starts 800 px down a 4,192 px page; 2 of 19 tables can be sorted; 10 rely on sideways scrolling on phones, which can hide dose or identity columns.
Proposed UX behaviour: A shared table controller hook for sort, filter and paging state (the pattern AGENTS.md section 4 already asks for), adopted one table at a time, audit log and staff first. Sort on the columns people sort by (name, time, wait). Paging above 50 rows. Under 768 px a table becomes stacked rows and never scrolls sideways with hidden columns that carry dose or identity. Numbers right-aligned with tabular numerals; the identifying cell bold and nothing else; one visible row action, the rest in a menu. Compact density (36 px rows) is an explicit per-table prop allowed only on the audit log, formulary, order sets and staff list; it is ignored on any device that reports a coarse pointer (any-pointer: coarse), and a destructive action inside a compact table (Offboard, Remove) stays 44 px or asks to confirm. AGENTS.md section 4 is amended in the same change, as the house rule requires for any row under 44 px.
Prototype and blueprint reference: docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md sections 4 and 9.
Components and tokens affected: table.tsx (density prop, stacked variant), a table controller in web/clinic/src/features/table, pagination. Density tokens.
Front end and back end split: Front end only. Server paging only where a list is already paged.
Prerequisites and blocked by: Blocked by the library-defaults and token tickets. Timing: after the first pilot weeks, or before the first staff training session if the founder moves it there; never between training and the first two pilot weeks (arbitration ruling 6).
Clinical sign-off: Question 20 of the validation plan (mouse or touch at the desk and in the office) informs it. Compact on any clinical list would need clinical sign-off and is not in scope.
Effort and regression risk: L · Medium: many tables; one table per pull request.
Deliberately NOT in this ticket: (1) Compact density on the patient directory, patient pickers, medicine lines, the front-desk list or any row that changes state (forbidden by ruling 2). (2) Virtual scrolling. (3) New table features nobody asked for.
ac:
- Given the density prop, when it is set on a table other than audit log, formulary, order sets or staff, then the build or lint fails
- Given a compact table on a device with a coarse pointer, when it renders, then rows are 48 px
- Given the audit log at 1440 by 900 with a mouse, when it opens, then at least 15 rows are visible and the table starts in the first 300 px
- Given staff and audit log, when a sortable header is used by keyboard, then the order changes, the sort state is announced, and lists over 50 rows are paged
- Given any table at 375 px, when it renders, then there is no sideways scrolling and no dose or identity field is hidden
- Given Offboard in the compact staff table, when it is measured, then it is at least 44 px or opens a confirmation
- Given AGENTS.md section 4, when this change merges, then it names the four tables and the coarse-pointer rule
- Given English and Arabic, when axe runs on each migrated table, then there is no violation and every scrollable region has a label
tests:
- Vitest: controller hook.
- Playwright: staff.spec.ts, audit-log.spec.ts, formulary.spec.ts with sort, paging and 375 stacked rows; a coarse-pointer emulation check.
notes:
- Regression risk: medium.

=== MDV-P2-055
title: Settings sub-navigation and small copy and state fixes: walk-in column name, Terms status, nurse-intake switch, organisation page
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E12
prd: P1-02
screens: F-08
priority: SHOULD
roles: Owner, Practice admin, Receptionist
labels: settings, ux, errors, navigation, epic: ux programme, track: design, wave: D3
estimate: 2
weeks: 13
depends: MDV-P1-086
confidence: 78 | Five small, separate fixes; the Terms one needs the Azure check from the redeploy ticket.
sources: docs/product-ux-audit/10-prioritized-implementation-backlog.md (audit backlog UX-34); docs/product-ux-audit/04-evidence-backed-findings.md (F-37, F-38, F-39, F-40, F-43); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-a-clinical-workflow.md (A-22, A-25, A-26); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-c-design-system.md (C-17); docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md (section 3)
desc:
Programme: MDV-P1-E12 · UX programme: safe, cohesive clinic workspace (from the Nov 2026 product UX audit). Track D (design rules and UI component setup), wave D3. This is audit backlog UX-34 of the Nov 2026 product UX audit (an audit id, not an MDV key).

Persona and route: /settings (all groups), walk-in success, /organisation · owner, practice admin, receptionist.
Findings and reviewers: F-37, F-38, F-39, F-40, F-43 · reviewers A-22, A-25, A-26, C-17. (F-41 has no ticket: see the epic. F-46 is in the Azure redeploy ticket.)
Rationale: Small things that make the product look unsure of itself: a success message that names the wrong column, a status that says booking is paused while booking works, a switch that changes everyone's board mid-day with no warning, a page that calls an endpoint answering 404, and two tab rows in two styles.
Proposed UX behaviour: Five fixes, each its own small change. (1) Walk-in success names the column the card is really in (Ready for doctor when nurse intake is off). (2) Settings → Terms: the status line matches what the server enforces; if the Azure check shows booking is not paused, the line is corrected, and if it should be paused, that is raised as a defect against the terms gate. (3) Switching nurse intake on or off asks to confirm and says what happens to patients now with the nurse. (4) /organisation for an approved clinic shows Approved with the date, or is hidden, and no longer calls an endpoint that answers 404. (5) Settings uses a left sub-navigation at 1024 px and wider in place of the second tab row; the five groups and the ?tab= addresses stay.
Prototype and blueprint reference: docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md section 3 (Settings).
Components and tokens affected: PageMessage, the existing Dialog, SegmentedControl or a nav list for settings. i18n keys.
Front end and back end split: Front end; (2) may turn out to be a back-end defect.
Prerequisites and blocked by: Blocked by the page components ticket. Timing: after the first pilot weeks, or before the first staff training session if the founder moves it there; never between training and the first two pilot weeks (arbitration ruling 6). Fixes 1, 3 and 4 are not renames and may land at any time.
Clinical sign-off: Not required.
Effort and regression risk: S each · Low.
Deliberately NOT in this ticket: (1) Regrouping settings panels. (2) Synthetic names on Azure (the redeploy ticket).
ac:
- Given nurse intake off, when a walk-in is checked in, then the success message names Ready for doctor
- Given Settings → Terms, when booking is allowed, then the status does not say booking is paused; when it is paused, then booking is refused by the server
- Given patients with the nurse, when the owner switches nurse intake off, then a dialog says how many are with the nurse and what happens to them, and nothing changes until confirmed
- Given an approved clinic, when /organisation opens, then no request answers 404 and the page says Approved or is not in the menu
- Given 1024 px and wider, when Settings opens, then a left sub-navigation replaces the second tab row and each ?tab= address opens the same panel as before
- Given English and Arabic, when axe runs on each changed screen, then there is no violation
tests:
- tests/e2e/front-desk.spec.ts (walk-in message), consents-terms.spec.ts, nurse-intake.spec.ts (switch dialog), organisation-state.spec.ts, settings-profile.spec.ts (sub-navigation).
notes:
- Regression risk: low.

=== MDV-P2-056
title: Truthful status and small motion: an Updated mark on live board changes, skeletons, an offline strip, named transition properties
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E12
prd: P0-07
priority: COULD
roles: Receptionist, Doctor, Nurse
labels: ui, a11y, realtime, design-system, epic: ux programme, track: design, wave: D3
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 14
depends: MDV-P1-082, MDV-P1-079, MDV-P1-095
confidence: 75 | Small and bounded by the blueprint's motion table; the never list is as important as the items.
sources: docs/product-ux-audit/10-prioritized-implementation-backlog.md (audit backlog UX-32); docs/product-ux-audit/04-evidence-backed-findings.md (F-36, F-47); docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md (section 12); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-b-visual-interaction.md (section 5, B-15, B-23, B-24); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-b-rebuttal.md (section 6); packages/ui/src/styles.css
desc:
Programme: MDV-P1-E12 · UX programme: safe, cohesive clinic workspace (from the Nov 2026 product UX audit). Track D (design rules and UI component setup), wave D3. This is audit backlog UX-32 of the Nov 2026 product UX audit (an audit id, not an MDV key).

Persona and route: Board, My day, schedule, patient record (skeletons and live mark); packages/ui switch, tabs, button.
Findings and reviewers: F-36, F-47 · reviewers B-15, B-23, B-24. WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.3 Status Messages for the live mark.
Rationale: A card changed by someone else arrives with no cue. Pages show a Loading sentence, then the layout appears and the height jumps (900 to 2,074 px on the board). The offline card covers the Done column and talks about recordings. No animation is needed; a few truthful status cues are.
Proposed UX behaviour: In this order. (1) Replace transition-all on Switch and Tabs with named properties and stop the focus ring fading in. (2) A board card or My day row changed by someone else gets the text tag Updated for 5 seconds and is announced in the existing live region; with motion allowed its background also fades from the brand tint to white over 1,200 ms; no movement. (3) Skeletons in the final layout for the board, My day, schedule and a record page: shown only after 200 ms, opacity pulse over 1,200 ms, static blocks under reduced motion. (4) Offline is a 40 px strip under the top bar with wording for the screen (Offline. The board shows the last update from 10:31. Actions are paused.). (5) The global reduced-motion rule allows colour and opacity changes up to 150 ms and no transforms. Never: page transitions, cards sliding between columns, staggered lists, animating the Ctrl+K search, anything that moves while a doctor types, animated counters, toasts over the patient strip.
Prototype and blueprint reference: docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md section 12 (the motion table and its values).
Components and tokens affected: New Skeleton in packages/ui; switch.tsx, tabs.tsx, button.tsx; the motion tokens; the connectivity banner.
Front end and back end split: Front end only.
Prerequisites and blocked by: Blocked by the SaveStatus ticket, the token ticket (motion values) and the board chrome ticket. Timing: after the first pilot weeks, or before the first staff training session if the founder moves it there; never between training and the first two pilot weeks (arbitration ruling 6). Item 2 may be pulled forward before the pilot if the device check shows two people share one board.
Clinical sign-off: Not required.
Effort and regression risk: S to M · Low, as long as nothing in the never list is added.
Deliberately NOT in this ticket: (1) Everything in the never list. (2) A motion library. (3) Press feedback and drawer animation beyond what Sheet already has.
ac:
- Given two people on one board, when one moves a card, then the other sees the tag Updated on that card for 5 seconds and a screen reader announces it once
- Given the Updated mark and the skeletons, when they play, then no element changes position, and under reduced motion there is no fade
- Given the board on a slow connection, when data arrives, then the layout height changes by less than 10 % from the skeleton
- Given the board offline, when the strip shows, then it names the last update time, covers no column and does not mention recordings
- Given a button, when it is focused by keyboard, then the ring is at full colour on the first frame, and no library component uses transition-all
- Given the change, when it is reviewed, then no page transition, sliding card, staggered list, animated counter or toast was added
- Given English and Arabic, when axe runs with skeletons and the strip showing, then there is no violation
tests:
- Playwright: two-context test on front-desk.spec.ts for the Updated tag; reduced-motion emulation; a layout-shift measure on the board.
- Vitest: Skeleton delay.
notes:
- Regression risk: low.

=== MDV-P2-057
title: Apply the type and width tokens: stray font sizes removed, body weight 500, page maximum 1,600 px, reading width, no sm:grid-cols
type: Task
epic: MDV-P1-E12
prd: P0-07
priority: SHOULD
roles: All staff roles
labels: design-system, ui, refactor, rtl, epic: ux programme, track: design, wave: D3
estimate: 3
weeks: 13
depends: MDV-P1-079, MDV-P1-078
confidence: 70 | A codemod to the nearest token plus a visual check in two languages; every screen is touched lightly.
sources: docs/product-ux-audit/10-prioritized-implementation-backlog.md (audit backlog UX-29); docs/product-ux-audit/04-evidence-backed-findings.md (F-21); docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md (sections 2 and 5); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-c-design-system.md (C-05, C-11, C-16, section 3.13 steps 7 and 9); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-b-visual-interaction.md (B-11, B-18); docs/product-ux-audit/evidence/local-metrics.jsonl
desc:
Programme: MDV-P1-E12 · UX programme: safe, cohesive clinic workspace (from the Nov 2026 product UX audit). Track D (design rules and UI component setup), wave D3. This is audit backlog UX-29 of the Nov 2026 product UX audit (an audit id, not an MDV key).

Persona and route: Every screen, lightly · all roles · 375 to 1920.
Findings and reviewers: F-21 · reviewers B-11, B-18, C-05, C-11, C-16. Part 2 of 2 of audit backlog UX-29 (part 1 defined the tokens).
Rationale: 12 rendered font sizes against a scale of 7; bold used 250 times and medium once, so weight ranks nothing; paragraphs up to 1,160 px wide; settings inputs 1,100 px; the sm: step is 360 px, so small-screen column rules apply on phones and clip the registration stepper at 375.
Proposed UX behaviour: A codemod moves arbitrary font sizes (11, 12.5, 13.5, 15, 17, 22 px) to the nearest type token; body weight becomes 500; bold stays for headings and the one thing that identifies a row; numbers, vitals, times and amounts use tabular numerals. Fluid pages get the 1,600 px maximum, descriptions and hints the reading width (about 72 characters), settings forms the 768 px form width. sm:grid-cols-* becomes md: and each changed layout is checked at 375. The ratchet counts for arbitrary font sizes and sm:grid-cols fall to zero and their lint rules turn to error (queue display and print stay on the allow-list).
Prototype and blueprint reference: docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md sections 2 and 5.
Components and tokens affected: No new component; uses the tokens of part 1.
Front end and back end split: Front end only.
Prerequisites and blocked by: Blocked by the token ticket and the control-height codemod. Merges alone, like the first codemod. Timing: after the first pilot weeks, or before the first staff training session if the founder moves it there; never between training and the first two pilot weeks (arbitration ruling 6).
Clinical sign-off: Not required. Typed clinical text stays 16 px.
Effort and regression risk: M · Medium: every screen changes slightly; checked by capture comparison in English and Arabic.
Deliberately NOT in this ticket: (1) A new typeface or palette. (2) Layout redesign of any screen.
ac:
- Given the 20 most-used screens at 1440, when rendered font sizes are measured, then only the nine token sizes appear (the queue display and print excepted)
- Given a list row, when it renders, then the identifying cell is bold and body text is weight 500
- Given 1920 px, when Today, the patient record and Settings render, then no paragraph is wider than about 72 characters and the page content is at most 1,600 px wide
- Given Register patient at 375 px, when the stepper renders, then no step label is clipped
- Given a feature file, when text-[13.5px] or sm:grid-cols-2 is added, then lint fails
- Given captures before and after in English and Arabic, when compared, then no text is truncated or overlapping, and axe finds no violation
tests:
- Metric check reusing the audit's font-size measure across the captured screens.
- J1 to J3 and feature suites green; capture comparison attached to the pull request.
notes:
- Regression risk: medium.

=== MDV-P2-058
title: Move the forms to Field and ErrorSummary, one feature at a time: registration first
