epic: MDV-P1-E12
prd: P1-05
screens: P-02
priority: SHOULD
roles: Receptionist, Practice admin, Owner
labels: registration, a11y, ui, settings, onboarding, epic: ux programme, track: design, wave: D3
estimate: 2.75
weeks: 14
depends: MDV-P1-085
confidence: 75 | Registration's own field is the base of the library one, so it moves first and cheaply; the others by hand.
sources: docs/product-ux-audit/10-prioritized-implementation-backlog.md (audit backlog UX-20); docs/product-ux-audit/04-evidence-backed-findings.md (F-23); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-b-visual-interaction.md (B-13, B-21); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-c-design-system.md (C-12, section 3.13 step 3)
desc:
Programme: MDV-P1-E12 · UX programme: safe, cohesive clinic workspace (from the Nov 2026 product UX audit). Track D (design rules and UI component setup), wave D3. This is audit backlog UX-20 of the Nov 2026 product UX audit (an audit id, not an MDV key).

Persona and route: /patients/new first; then settings, onboarding, the pregnancy card, sign-up, the platform console · receptionist, admin, owner.
Findings and reviewers: F-23 · reviewers B-13, B-21, C-12. Part 2 of 2 of audit backlog UX-20.
Rationale: After an empty submit on registration, focus stays on the button and at 375 px the errors are off screen. The pregnancy card's message is generic and not linked to a field.
Proposed UX behaviour: One feature per pull request, in this order: registration, settings, onboarding and sign-up, the pregnancy card, the platform console. Each form uses Field for every control and shows ErrorSummary after a failed submit, with focus on it. Each form picks one required or optional convention. Buttons that were disabled from the start with no reason (Check in now on walk-in) are enabled and validate on press, or show the reason beside them. The duplicate block at registration and the identity confirmation at check-in are untouched. The ratchet count for local Field components falls to zero and the lint rule turns to error.
Prototype and blueprint reference: docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md section 9.
Components and tokens affected: Field, ErrorSummary. Removes five local Field wrappers.
Front end and back end split: Front end only. Zod schemas stay in domain.
Prerequisites and blocked by: Blocked by the Field and ErrorSummary component ticket. Timing: after the first pilot weeks, or before the first staff training session if the founder moves it there; never between training and the first two pilot weeks (arbitration ruling 6).
Clinical sign-off: Not required. The duplicate block and identity confirmation must not change (do-not-change list).
Effort and regression risk: M · Medium: registration is on the walk-in path; its click count is re-measured.
Deliberately NOT in this ticket: (1) Changing any validation rule or required field. (2) Date pickers in the app language.
ac:
- Given Register patient submitted empty at 375 px and 1440 px, when the submit fails, then focus is on the summary, it is in the viewport, and each link moves focus to its field
- Given each migrated form, when it renders, then required or optional is marked one way throughout, in words
- Given walk-in before a patient is chosen, when Check in now is pressed or read, then the reason is stated in words
- Given registration and check-in, when a duplicate or an identity confirmation applies, then they behave exactly as before, and the walk-in path is at most 6 clicks new and 3 returning
- Given features, when searched, then no local Field component remains and the lint rule is an error
- Given English and Arabic, when axe runs on each migrated form with errors showing, then there is no violation
tests:
- tests/e2e/registration.spec.ts, registration-full.spec.ts, settings-profile.spec.ts, onboarding.spec.ts, platform-console.spec.ts: failed submit → focus on summary.
- J1 step 2 and J3 step 1 green.
notes:
- Regression risk: medium.

=== MDV-P2-059
title: Adopt PageHeader, Card and Section, PageMessage and EmptyState across the clinic app and the platform console
type: Task
epic: MDV-P1-E12
prd: P0-07
priority: SHOULD
roles: All staff roles
labels: design-system, ui, refactor, epic: ux programme, track: design, wave: D3
estimate: 3
weeks: 12-13
depends: MDV-P1-084, MDV-P1-086
confidence: 75 | Mostly codemod: seven of the ten Message functions are near-identical.
sources: docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md (sections 2, 7 and 14); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-c-design-system.md (C-04, C-22, section 2.2, section 3.13 step 2); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-b-visual-interaction.md (B-10, B-16, B-22, B-26); docs/product-ux-audit/04-evidence-backed-findings.md (F-19, F-44)
desc:
Programme: MDV-P1-E12 · UX programme: safe, cohesive clinic workspace (from the Nov 2026 product UX audit). Track D (design rules and UI component setup), wave D3. No audit backlog id. Created from the audit's rulings and blueprint, not from a backlog line (see Findings).

Persona and route: Every page title, card surface and page-level message · web/clinic and web/platform-admin.
Findings and reviewers: F-19, F-44 · reviewers B-10, B-16, B-22, B-26, C-04, C-22. From the blueprint's Next list and guardrails; no UX number of its own in the backlog.
Rationale: 37 hand-written page titles at seven different heights, 97 inline card strings, 10 local Message functions. The platform console does not use the shared page header, so library fixes do not reach it; its sign-in overflows at 375 px.
Proposed UX behaviour: Every page uses PageHeader (one 44 px row; content starts at about 124 px); the small label above the title goes where it only repeats the menu item; the date is secondary text, not part of the title. Inline card strings become Card or Section in the two sizes; no bordered card inside a bordered card. The local Message and Empty functions become PageMessage and EmptyState. The platform console adopts PageContainer and PageHeader, and its sign-in no longer overflows at 375 px. On the patients directory, search and filters sit on one 44 px row and repeated cell labels go. The ratchet counts for raw h1, border bg-card, and local Message, Card and Empty fall to zero and the lint rules turn to error.
Prototype and blueprint reference: docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md sections 2 and 7.
Components and tokens affected: PageHeader, Card, Section, PageMessage, EmptyState.
Front end and back end split: Front end only. By codemod where identical, by hand elsewhere; one feature group per pull request.
Prerequisites and blocked by: Blocked by the shell components and page components tickets. Timing: after the first pilot weeks, or before the first staff training session if the founder moves it there; never between training and the first two pilot weeks (arbitration ruling 6). Where a track S or wave D2 ticket already touches a file, it replaces that file's local Message or Card itself.
Clinical sign-off: Not required.
Effort and regression risk: M · Medium: page titles are test locators in many specs.
Deliberately NOT in this ticket: (1) Renaming any page (the names ticket). (2) Layout redesign.
ac:
- Given every page in both apps at 1440, when the title is measured, then it sits in a 44 px header row at the same height and content starts within 130 px of the top
- Given the board and My day, when data loads, then the title and actions do not move
- Given features, when the ratchet runs, then raw h1, border bg-card, and local Message, Card and Empty are all zero and their lint rules are errors
- Given the platform console sign-in at 375 px, when it renders, then page width equals viewport width and controls are at least 44 px
- Given the patients directory at 1024 by 768, when it opens, then the first row starts at or above 300 px
- Given English and Arabic, when axe runs on each migrated page, then there is no violation and each page has one h1
tests:
- tests/e2e/page-layout.spec.ts extended: header position on every route.
- platform-console.spec.ts at 375.
- All suites green per feature group.
notes:
- Regression risk: medium.

=== MDV-P2-060
title: Adopt Chip, Tag, Banner and SegmentedControl in features: one chip vocabulary, one view switch
type: Task
epic: MDV-P1-E12
prd: P0-07
priority: SHOULD
roles: All staff roles
labels: design-system, ui, refactor, clinical, epic: ux programme, track: design, wave: D3
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 13-14
depends: MDV-P1-083, MDV-P1-086
confidence: 75 | About 12 chip variants and 20 view switches to replace by hand; looks change slightly, on purpose.
sources: docs/product-ux-audit/10-prioritized-implementation-backlog.md (audit backlog UX-21); docs/product-ux-audit/04-evidence-backed-findings.md (F-19); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-c-design-system.md (C-04, section 2.2); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-b-visual-interaction.md (B-08, B-09, B-19)
desc:
Programme: MDV-P1-E12 · UX programme: safe, cohesive clinic workspace (from the Nov 2026 product UX audit). Track D (design rules and UI component setup), wave D3. This is audit backlog UX-21 of the Nov 2026 product UX audit (an audit id, not an MDV key).

Persona and route: Every status label and view switch · all roles.
Findings and reviewers: F-19, F-20 · reviewers B-08, B-09, B-19, C-04. Part 3 of 3 of audit backlog UX-21.
Rationale: Three chip styles sit side by side on one Today row; the same switch-the-view interaction has five appearances and its selected state relies on a thicker border.
Proposed UX behaviour: The local Chips, SafetyChip, SourceChip, LicenceBadge, VerificationTag, StateLabel, AppointmentChip and the inline rounded-full spans become Chip or Tag with a tone. The 20 hand-built view switches become SegmentedControl; settings sections keep one tab style; filters (directory, patient record) become chips with a tick when on. One primary (filled) button per view: on My day the row buttons are outline when the next-patient card already holds the action. Wording of every status stays the same. The allergy uses AllergyBlock wherever it appears.
Prototype and blueprint reference: docs/product-ux-audit/08-design-system-blueprint.md sections 6 and 7.
Components and tokens affected: Chip, Tag, Banner, SegmentedControl, AllergyBlock.
Front end and back end split: Front end only; one feature group per pull request.
Prerequisites and blocked by: Blocked by the Chip, Tag and Banner ticket and the page components ticket. Timing: after the first pilot weeks, or before the first staff training session if the founder moves it there; never between training and the first two pilot weeks (arbitration ruling 6).
Clinical sign-off: The allergy look was agreed in part 2 (question 4). Any change to a clinical status wording is out of scope.
Effort and regression risk: M · Medium: visible on every screen; status wording must not change.
Deliberately NOT in this ticket: (1) New statuses or wording. (2) Compact chips.
ac:
- Given a My day row with three states, when it renders, then all three use Chip or Tag from the library
- Given the board, My day, schedule, registration and the consultation, when each view switch renders, then it is SegmentedControl with the selected state exposed to assistive technology
- Given every status label before and after, when the translated strings are compared, then none changed
- Given the chart, the consultation, the Add medicine dialog and the sign dialog, when the allergy renders, then it is AllergyBlock in each
- Given My day and the board, when the first viewport is counted, then at most one filled primary button shows
- Given English and Arabic, when axe runs, then there is no violation and no status relies on colour alone
tests:
- Feature suites updated per group; capture comparison in en and ar attached.
- today.spec.ts: one primary button in the first viewport.
notes:
- Regression risk: medium.

=== MDV-P2-061
title: Patient record and list chrome found only in the reviewers' reports: empty sections collapse, one-row filters, sideways scrolling inside tables
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E12
prd: P2-02
screens: E-01
priority: COULD
roles: Doctor, Receptionist
labels: chart, patients, ui, responsive, epic: ux programme, track: design, wave: D3
estimate: 2
weeks: 14
depends: MDV-P1-086, MDV-P1-083
confidence: 72 | Small layout fixes with measurements to hit; none was in the consolidated findings, so priority is the lowest.
sources: docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-b-visual-interaction.md (B-04, B-16, B-17, B-19, B-21); docs/product-ux-audit/reviews/reviewer-c-design-system.md (C-10); docs/product-ux-audit/05-accessibility-responsive-and-reliability.md (By breakpoint)
desc:
Programme: MDV-P1-E12 · UX programme: safe, cohesive clinic workspace (from the Nov 2026 product UX audit). Track D (design rules and UI component setup), wave D3. No audit backlog id. Created from the audit's rulings and blueprint, not from a backlog line (see Findings).

Persona and route: /patients/:id (patient record), the schedule appointment panel, the prescription table at narrow widths · doctor, receptionist.
Findings and reviewers: No consolidated finding number. Reviewer findings B-17, B-21, and the prescription table part of B-04 and C-10, which the audit's backlog did not turn into a ticket. Found while checking every reviewer finding against the tickets.
Rationale: The patient record is 3,241 to 5,129 px tall and the doctor scrolls past six Not recorded tiles to reach the medicines; its pinned filter takes 156 px of a phone. A completed visit's panel shows four disabled actions with the same reason four times. The prescription table needs 1,000 px and scrolls sideways inside itself from 768 to 1023 px, hiding dose columns.
Proposed UX behaviour: Patient record: an empty section collapses to one line with its add action (Vitals: none recorded · Add); the filter chips are one sideways-scrolling row of 52 px; link buttons align to the text edge. Appointment panel: for a completed visit the four actions are replaced by one line, This visit is completed. Prescription lines from 768 to 1023 px render as stacked rows (medicine, dose, frequency, duration each visible) and never scroll sideways inside the table. Unknown values stay Not recorded in words; nothing is guessed or hidden.
Prototype and blueprint reference: None. Reviewer B, screen-by-screen critique.
Components and tokens affected: Card, Chip, the Table stacked variant when the table ticket has landed (before that, a local stacked layout for the prescription lines).
Front end and back end split: Front end only.
Prerequisites and blocked by: Blocked by the page components and chip tickets. Timing: after the first pilot weeks, or before the first staff training session if the founder moves it there; never between training and the first two pilot weeks (arbitration ruling 6).
Clinical sign-off: Ask the pilot doctor in passing whether collapsed empty sections hide anything they rely on; not a merge gate. Not recorded must still be visible as words for allergies in every case.
Effort and regression risk: M · Low. The allergy state is never collapsed.
Deliberately NOT in this ticket: (1) Changing section order on the patient record. (2) The patient record's life-stage modules.
ac:
- Given a patient with six empty sections at 1440 by 900, when the record opens, then each empty section is one line with its add action and the medicines start within the first two viewports
- Given allergies not recorded, when the record renders, then the allergy block is shown in full with its words
- Given 375 px, when the record scrolls, then the pinned filter is at most 56 px tall
- Given a completed visit's panel, when it opens, then one line says the visit is completed and no disabled button repeats a reason
- Given a prescription with three lines at 768 px, when it renders, then dose, frequency and duration of every line are visible with no sideways scrolling
- Given English and Arabic, when axe runs, then there is no violation
tests:
- tests/e2e/patient-360.spec.ts, schedule.spec.ts, prescription.spec.ts and tablet.spec.ts with the measures above.
notes:
- Regression risk: low.
